From e4d89951ddc2958428e8dbde033c807b076906d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sully <sully.niu@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:22:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] net: phy: motorcomm: reapply YT8531 clock output
 configuration on config_init

The YT8531 clock output is configured from .probe() only, which runs once
when the PHY is probed. Taking the MAC interface down and up stops and
restarts the PHY, and the configuration is never re-applied, so the clock
output stays disabled from then on.

On boards that use the PHY as the RGMII reference clock source (no
st,eth-clk-sel property, so the MAC takes its TX clock from the PHY's
CLK125 output), losing that clock disables transmission completely: the
MAC reports register access timeouts and no frame reaches the wire, while
reception keeps working because it uses the PHY's RX_CLK.

Extract the configuration into yt8531_clk_config() and call it from
yt8531_config_init() as well. config_init runs on every phy_init_hw(),
i.e. on probe, attach and resume, which is where this kind of hardware
configuration belongs. The YT8521 family already handles its clock output
on that path.

Reproducer on an STM32MP25 board with a YT8531 in RGMII mode:

    # ip link set end0 down && sleep 2 && ip link set end0 up
    # ping -c 3 192.168.156.151
    From 192.168.156.153 icmp_seq=1 Destination Host Unreachable
    # dmesg | grep Timeout
    stm32-dwmac 482d0000.eth2 end0: Timeout accessing MAC_VLAN_Tag_Filter

Transmission only recovers after a reboot.
---
 drivers/net/phy/motorcomm.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/phy/motorcomm.c b/drivers/net/phy/motorcomm.c
index 7a11fdb68..0b47c53c1 100755
--- a/drivers/net/phy/motorcomm.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/motorcomm.c
@@ -1072,7 +1072,7 @@ static int yt8521_probe(struct phy_device *phydev)
 					  val);
 }
 
-static int yt8531_probe(struct phy_device *phydev)
+static int yt8531_clk_config(struct phy_device *phydev)
 {
 	struct device_node *node = phydev->mdio.dev.of_node;
 	u16 mask, val;
@@ -1109,6 +1109,11 @@ static int yt8531_probe(struct phy_device *phydev)
 					  val);
 }
 
+static int yt8531_probe(struct phy_device *phydev)
+{
+	return yt8531_clk_config(phydev);
+}
+
 /**
  * ytphy_utp_read_lpa() - read LPA then setup lp_advertising for utp
  * @phydev: a pointer to a &struct phy_device
@@ -1610,6 +1615,10 @@ static int yt8531_config_init(struct phy_device *phydev)
 	struct device_node *node = phydev->mdio.dev.of_node;
 	int ret;
 
+	ret = yt8531_clk_config(phydev);
+	if (ret < 0)
+		return ret;
+
 	ret = ytphy_rgmii_clk_delay_config_with_lock(phydev);
 	if (ret < 0)
 		return ret;
-- 
